{"id":"121ea2e24c75ec11","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-consistency-strength.md","title":"Relative Consistency Strength","display":"df-consistency-strength — Relative Consistency Strength","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-consistency-strength","aliases":["58-df-consistency-strength"],"display":"df-consistency-strength — Relative Consistency Strength","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-consistency]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-consistency-strength"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-consistency-strength</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-consistency-strength — Relative Consistency Strength"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6996aaff4caeacce\" href=\"?note=6996aaff4caeacce\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-consistency\">../batch13/58-df-consistency</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,U,\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\in V\">\\(T,U,\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\in V\\)</span> (theories, signature, proof system, and contradiction formula)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S\\)</span> (explicit syntactic consistency predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6996aaff4caeacce\" href=\"?note=6996aaff4caeacce\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-consistency\">../batch13/58-df-consistency</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ConsistencyStrengthLeq}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{ConsistencyStrengthLeq}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> (relative-consistency comparison defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}consistency\\text{-}strength}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\operatorname{ConsistencyStrengthLeq}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(T,U,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\leftrightarrow\\bigl(\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S(U,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\to\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S(T,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}consistency\\text{-}strength}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\operatorname{ConsistencyStrengthLeq}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(T,U,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\leftrightarrow\\bigl(\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S(U,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\to\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S(T,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The displayed relation says that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> has at least the consistency strength of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>, relative to the same explicit signature, proof system, and contradiction formula.</li>\n<li>The implication is evaluated in the ambient metatheory; it is not an implication internal to either object theory.</li>\n<li>A displayed list of large-cardinal names is not itself a consistency-strength relation, and large-cardinal notions should not be forced into an unsupported linear order.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-consistency","status":"resolved","id":"6996aaff4caeacce","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-consistency]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-consistency","status":"resolved","id":"6996aaff4caeacce","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S$ (explicit syntactic consistency predicate, see [[../batch13/58-df-consistency]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,U,\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ConsistencyStrengthLeq}_{\\mathrm{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}consistency\\text{-}strength}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\operatorname{ConsistencyStrengthLeq}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(T,U,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\leftrightarrow\\bigl(\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S(U,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\to\\operatorname{ConsistentTheory}_S(T,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false}],"bytes":1464,"backlinks":[{"id":"83107a17d9417d6d","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ConsistencyStrengthLeq}_{\\mathrm{meta}}:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ is the relative-consistency relation with explicit proof system, signature, and contradiction formula (see [[58-df-consistency-strength]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-352","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-consistency-strength.md|58-df-consistency-strength]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["6996aaff4caeacce"]}